an5.31:12.1 starts: so the Perfectly Enlightened One’s disciple,
an5.31:12.2 starts: the wise one accomplished in vision,
an5.31:12.3 starts: surpasses the miserly person
an5.31:12.4 starts: in five specific respects:
an5.32:8.1 starts: For those confident in regard to the foremost,
an5.32:8.2 starts: knowing the foremost Dhamma,
an5.32:8.3 starts: confident in the Buddha—the foremost—
an5.32:8.4 starts: unsurpassed, worthy of offerings;
an5.33:9.1 starts: She does not despise her husband,
an5.33:9.2 starts: the man who constantly supports her,
an5.33:9.3 starts: who ardently and eagerly
an5.33:9.4 starts: always brings her whatever she wants.
an5.33:10.1 starts: Nor does a good woman scold her husband
an5.33:10.2 starts: with speech caused by jealousy;
an5.33:10.3 starts: the wise woman shows veneration
an5.33:10.4 starts: to all those whom her husband reveres.
an5.34:8.1 starts: By giving, he becomes dear and many resort
an5.34:8.2 starts: He attains a good reputation and his fame
an5.34:8.3 starts: The generous man is composed
an5.34:8.4 starts: and confidently enters the assembly.
an5.38:3.1 starts: A large tree with a mighty trunk,
an5.38:3.2 starts: branches, leaves, and fruit,
an5.38:3.3 starts: firm roots, and bearing fruit,
an5.38:3.4 starts: is a support for many birds.
an5.38:4.1 starts: Having flown across the sky,
an5.38:4.2 starts: the birds resort to this delightful base:
an5.38:4.3 starts: those in need of shade partake of its
an5.38:4.4 starts: those needing fruit enjoy its fruit.
an5.38:6.1 starts: those in the world who are fields of
an5.38:6.2 starts: devoid of lust and hatred,
an5.38:6.3 starts: devoid of delusion, taintless—
an5.38:6.4 starts: resort to such a person.
an5.40:2.1 starts: Just as the trees that grow
an5.40:2.2 starts: in dependence on a rocky mountain
an5.40:2.3 starts: in a vast forest wilderness
an5.40:2.4 starts: might become great ‘woodland lords,’
